%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

\section{Conclusions}

In this paper we have shown that {\sc Directed Metric Dimension} is decidable in linear time for directed co-graphs and we also presented an algorithm to compute minimum resolving sets for directed co-graphs in linear time. Additionally, we have shown that {\sc Directed Metric Dimension} is NP-complete for DAGs, extending the existing results for general directed and oriented graphs.

The metric dimension as well as its variants have rarely been studied for directed graphs \cite{SW21}. Developing efficient algorithms to compute the metric dimension for specific graph classes is one of the most interesting challenges to us.

