codex
The adversary sweep is behaving as intended so far: incidence outliers, greedy choice, bounded min-conflicts, and the exact propagated DPLL all fail on the tested hard seeds. The DPLL reaches its 1,000-node cap in roughly 4–8 seconds per instance, so the baseline is a measured failed search rather than a cardinality claim.
codex
The full revised selftest is now underway with all 8 shipping seeds. The spot sweep completed cleanly: min-conflicts failed 8/8, and exact DPLL failed 8/8 only after exhausting 1,000 nodes on each instance (roughly 3.9–7.9 seconds per seed). I’m waiting for the complete G1–G9 report, including the 20-seed canonicalization test, before accepting this Track A replacement.
