-Attack defenses.  In every four-clause parity block each literal occurs exactly
-twice, so per-literal frequency is identically balanced and planted/other
-literal labels have the same marginal distribution.  The cycle order, ground
-labels, pair order, set order, and within-set order are independently shuffled.
-Selftest measures a frequency outlier probe, greedy marginal coverage, 256
-structure-aware random restarts, and a branch-free one-pass repair heuristic.
-The successful Gaussian algorithm is reported separately, as Track B requires.
 
-Canonicalization.  Arbitrary ground relabeling, pair reordering, family-set
-reordering, and within-set reordering are genuine symmetries.  Exact canonical
-labeling of the associated incidence structure is a graph-isomorphism problem;
-the key therefore uses an invariant Weisfeiler--Leman refinement fingerprint.
-The selftest checks the symmetries and carried witnesses over twenty seeds and
-checks twenty unrelated instances for distinct keys.  WL collisions remain a
-documented theoretical caveat rather than being concealed by hashing the seed.
