- Canonical-key tests: 60/60 invariant transformations and 20/20 unrelated instances distinct.
- Shipping answer: 120 characters, 33 atoms, approximately 30 tokens.
- Intended route: 210 operations.

The generator is theorem-backed by the DAG NP-completeness construction in the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.08594), while explicitly avoiding its linear-time directed co-graph regime.

The only incomplete requirement is the external oracle verdict. All three harness runs received OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded”; these are recorded as API errors, not solver failures. Consequently the result is locally complete but must not be submitted as hardened until the oracle arms are rerun.
