The next lemma shows that there is no vertex $v \in V(G_{\hat{w}}) \setminus \{u_1,u_2\}$ such that $G_{\hat{w}}$ neither has a 1-vertex nor a 2-vertex w.r.t.\ $R_{\hat{w}} \cup \{v\}$. That is, $u_1$ and $u_2$ are the only possible double removers. This shows that we only need to consider a 1-vertex or a 2-vertex to remove a 1-vertex or 2-vertex of $G_{\hat{w}}$ w.r.t.\ a resolving set $R_{\hat{w}}$, see \Cref{figure6}.

