README.md:1:# arXiv:2306.08594 — directed resolving sets in DAGs
README.md:18:Schmitz and Wanke’s [*The directed metric dimension of directed co-graphs*](https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.08594) defines a directed resolving set using distances **from** selected vertices. Its final section proves that Directed Metric Dimension is NP-complete even for directed acyclic graphs by transforming a Hitting Set family into a layered DAG.
README.md:24:The theorem in the paper’s “Directed acyclic graphs” section gives the relevant worst-case result: the reduction preserves a Hitting Set of size `k` as a resolving set of size `k+3`. The shipping preset has 30 growing choice groups, eight values per group, 180 balanced NAE rows, 390 Hitting Set members, and a normal-form space of `8^30`. Plants and decoys have exactly equal incidence frequency because every row is paired with its complement and every group appears once per regular round.
README.md:26:The strongest implemented baseline is q-ary DPLL with MRV and NAE unit propagation. Its worst case is `O(q^groups)`. At shipping size it exhausted 1,000 nodes in **6.557 s** on the G5 instance without solving; across eight G6 seeds it exhausted 8,000 nodes in **50.422 s** and solved 0/8. Incidence outlier, one-pass greedy, and bounded min-conflicts attacks also solved 0/8.
README.md:78:| easy | 4 | 18 | 9 | 72 | 126 | 327 | 21 | oracle not reached: key limit |
README.md:80:| hard | 8 | 30 | 18 | 240 | 390 | 1,023 | 33 | provisional shipping preset |
README.md:91:| G4 | pass | 0/200,000 structure-aware guesses from `8^30` candidates |
README.md:92:| G5 | pass | shipping observed density 0/200,000; DPLL 1,000 nodes, 6.557 s, unsolved; demo has exactly 4/8 answers |
README.md:96:| G9(c) | pass | 120 chars, 30 estimated tokens, 33 atoms, 210 intended operations |
README.md:106:| easy | Claude Sonnet 5 | 699533121 | error | redraw; same HTTP 403 |
README.md:107:| easy | Claude Sonnet 5 | 1832682486 | error | redraw; same HTTP 403; harness stopped |
README.md:117:The hinted-minus-placebo diagnostic is unavailable; the numeric `0.0` in `selftest_report.json` is only the zero-attempt sentinel and supports no conclusion about the stated intuition. The structural hint names only the same-layer signature invariant. The size/effort arm passes at 120 characters, 33 atoms, and 210 operations.
