codex
A scaling check caught one more issue before handoff: at the fourth post-`hard` escalation, the paper’s reduction requires more set layers than ground vertices, and the old code raised instead of applying the paper’s own “duplicate sets if necessary” normalization. I’m implementing that normalization symbolically, so escalation remains valid without lengthening the answer or adding post-insight checks.
