 ## Caveats
 
-The theorem proves worst-case NP-completeness for DAGs; it does **not** prove this balanced planted distribution hard. The 0/200,000 result is an observed rate under the precise prior “uniformly choose one displayed value per group”; it is not a confidence proof that every informed strategy has probability below `1e-6`. The exact baseline is node-capped, so it shows that this particular search prefix is costly, not that uncapped DPLL never finishes.
