codex
Final validation is clean: deterministic generation, JSON round-trip, no import-time output, default render without hints, all four presets, six escalation rounds, report consistency, and all three transcript schemas check. The only unmet requirement is external rather than mathematical or code-level: every OpenRouter call returned HTTP 403, so no multi-vendor hardness verdict can honestly be claimed.
codex
Implemented and locally verified a Track A generator based on the paper’s Section 3 Hitting Set → DAG reduction. The title-class construction was avoided because Section 2, Theorem 1 solves directed co-graphs in linear time; Section 3, Theorem 2 supplies the NP-complete DAG regime. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.08594)

Deliverables:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2306.08594/gen_2306_08594.py:1)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2306.08594/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2306.08594/README.md:1)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2306.08594/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Structural-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2306.08594/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2306.08594/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- All G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- Random guesses: 0/200,000.
- Four attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Standard DPLL baseline: 160,000 aggregate nodes, 72.013 seconds, unsolved.
- Shipping answer: 142 characters, 39 atoms.
- Intended route: 288 checks.
- Six escalation rounds build and verify successfully.

The external hardening requirement remains incomplete: all twelve bare/hinted/placebo calls returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.” The script-owned error evidence is preserved and is not misreported as oracle failure. Consequently, the module is locally verified but remains provisional and should not be submitted until the hardening runs succeed.
