406,922
Implemented the verified Track A generator using the paper’s Theorem 2 Hitting Set → DAG reduction. Theorem 1’s linear-time directed co-graph regime was correctly excluded.

Local results:

- All G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- Structure-aware guesses: 0/200,000 in a \(10^{36}\) space.
- Four attacks: 0/8 each.
- DPLL baseline: 20,000 nodes and 9.127 seconds.
- Answer: 152 characters, 39 atoms.
- Exact symbolic verification cross-checked against explicit graph BFS.

I also corrected a subtle reduction issue by adding an unused first ground vertex, preventing source `b` from accidentally resolving a missed set-layer pair.

